$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure A mixture of DMF (2.00 mL, 25.8 mmol) and 10 M KOH
(0.500 mL, 5.00 mmol) was heated at reflux for 5 min. The corresponding
aryl halide (1.00 mmol) was added and the resulting mixture was heated
for 0.5 h at 95 °C. The mixture was treated with additional 10 M KOH
(0.500 mL, 5.00 mmol) and heated for an additional 0.5 h. The reaction
was monitored by TLC and additional portions of 10 M KOH (0.500 mL, 5.00
mmol) were added in 0.5-h intervals until completion was evident. The
reaction mixture was then cooled, diluted with water, and vacuum filtered
(for solid products) or extracted (for product oils) with Et2O (3x). For
reaction products that were extracted, the organic fractions were
combined, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and concentrated under reduced
pressure to give the final product. N, N-dimethyl-2, 4-dinitrobenzenamine
(Table 2, entry 1). Using General Procedure A, 2,4-dinitrofluorobenzene
(190 mg, 0.130 mL, 1.00 mmol) underwent conversion after stirring for 3
min at 95 °C. The product crystallized from the reaction mixture and was
collected by vacuum filtration and washed with ice cold water (10.0 mL).
N,N-dimethyl-2,4-dinitrobenzenamine (171 mg, 81%) as a yellow crystalline
powder. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 8.67 (d, J=2.8 Hz, 1H), 8.21 (dd,
J=2.8, 9.5 Hz, 1H), 7.00 (d, J=9.5 Hz, 1H), 3.05 (s, 6H).[1]
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM incremental addition of agent in 0.5h intervals in stage 3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM General method for nucleophilic aromatic substitution of aryl fluorides
and chlorides with dimethylamine using hydroxide-assisted decomposition
of N,N-dimethylformamide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Garcia, Juana; Sorrentino, Jacob; Diller, Emily J.; Chapman, Daniel;
Woydziak, Zachary R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2016), 46(5), 475-481

