$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the MCR toward Annulated
Quinazolinones (4{1,1,1}-4{1,2,10}) and α-Aminoamides
(5{1,1,4}-5{1,1,5}). Under argon atmosphere the respective imine (1.00
equiv.), dissolved in anhydrous DCM (3 mL per mmol imine), was cooled
down to 0 °C. A solution of the respective acyl chloride (1.10 equiv.) in
anhydrous DCM (2 mL per mmol imine) was added dropwise. After stirring
overnight at rt Et3N (2.50 equiv.) was added dropwise and the reaction
mixture stirred for a further hour. Then the respective amine (1.50
equiv.) was added dropwise at 0 °C. After stirring overnight at rt the
solution was poured into icewater (6 mL per mmol imine). The organic
layer was separated and the aqueous phase was extracted with DCM (3 × 3
mL per mmol imine). The combined organic layers were washed with a
saturated aqueous solution of NaHCO3 (1 × 5 mL per mmol imine), H2O (1 ×
5 mL per mmol imine) and dried over MgSO4. The solvent was removed on a
rotary evaporator. The purification of the resulting crude product is
specified below for individual cases.
(RS)-4-Allyl-1,1,3,3-tetramethyl-7-nitro-3a,4-dihydro-1H-thiazolo[4,3-b]quinazolin-9(3H)-one
(4{1,1,1}). Prepared from 3-thiazoline 1{1} (286 mg, 2.00 mmol), acyl
chloride 2{1} (448 mg, 2.20 mmol), Et3N (506 mg, 5.00 mmol) and
allylamine 3{1} (171 mg, 3.00 mmol). The crude product was purified by
recrystallization from n-hexane/DCM.
(RS)-4’-Allyl-5’-bromo-3’,3’-dimethyl-7’-nitro-3a’,4’-dihydrospiro-[cyclohexane-1,1’-oxazolo-[4,3-b]quinazoline]-9’(3’H)-one
(4{5,2,1}). Prepared from 3-oxazoline 1{5} (334 mg, 2.00 mmol), acyl
chloride 2{2} (621 mg, 2.20 mmol), Et3N (506 mg, 5.00 mmol) and
allylamine 3{1} (171 mg, 3.00 mmol). The crude product was purified by
column chromatography using DCM. 730 mg of a yellow solid (81%). Rf =
0.63; Mp: 187-189 °C. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.80 (d, J = 2.7 Hz,
1H), 8.48 (d, J = 2.7 Hz, 1H), 5.75-5.67 (m, 1H), 5.28-5.26 (m, 1H),
5.25-5.24 (m, 1H), 4.78 (s, 1H), 4.74-4.70 (m, 1H), 3.76-3.72 (m, 1H),
2.80-2.74 (m, 1H), 2.16-2.10 (m, 1H), 1.70-1.57 (m, 6H), 1.51-1.47 (m,
1H), 1.43 (s, 3H), 1.33-1.24 (m, 1H), 1.11 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (126 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 157.3, 151.6, 142.0, 133.8, 131.9, 124.2, 122.9, 120.9, 112.3,
94.0, 80.2, 79.3, 57.3, 36.2, 34.3, 26.6, 24.9, 23.3, 22.4, 22.2. HRMS
(ESI-TOF) m/z: calcd for C20H24BrN3NaO4 [M + Na]+ 472.0848, found
472.0850. IR: ν 3093, 2968, 2936, 2856, 1667, 1592, 1489, 1461, 1429,
1408, 1328, 1259, 1229, 1167, 1097, 996, 910, 775, 745 cm-1.
